{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01fff8f48cfd83b2d578996650ef2352dae6fd070374817e1016f38bdc538242", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following two lemmas provide the most used and most useful\ncharacterizations of relatively very ample and relatively ample\ninvertible sheaves when the morphism is of finite type.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8ce82b52fbf4fc55df5d790381c1450360226d70441235a053ee0d11581cc495", "unit_id": "tag:02NO:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$S = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0008": "$j$", "MATH_0009": "$n_j$", "MATH_0010": "$$\ni_j :\nX_j = f^{-1}(V_j) = V_j \\times_S X\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{P}^{n_j}_{V_j}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{L}|_{X_j} \\cong i_j^*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}^{n_j}_{V_j}}(1)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-very-ample-on-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:90cb8a6f56598c10a67ca625d59699f4906ca2ba97361154fb09f03c285db6f4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bac2cfc06814bacf5099de798292b5563cae2149507773a5238de35d8ccb984c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible sheaf on <MATH_0003>.\nAssume <MATH_0004> is of finite type.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is <MATH_0006>-relatively very ample, and\n<STRUCT_0003> there exist an open covering <MATH_0007>,\nfor each <MATH_0008> an integer <MATH_0009>, and immersions\n<MATH_0010>\nover <MATH_0011> such that\n<MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:942d806d1c3ec4abfb0b4a63c15b9dcc68df368120eec7d43e72a948e909c2fb", "unit_id": "tag:02NQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-very-ample-finite-type-over-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-relatively-very-ample}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ec0acf6913c58f1a1b84f7a68677f9dc6303859437a676d3633f71bd285d723a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1335209a71b958c9cc007dc04a4fbd0ef02bb5343540ce24f065dfa593f09146", "source_text": "We see that (1) implies (2) by taking an affine open covering of <MATH_0001>\nand applying Lemma <REF_0001> to\neach of the restrictions of <MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003>. We see that (2) implies (1) by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c8b6e8275715e27f8934fe390084b1e7c4fdb65b96288a15a89ac457d5d301d", "unit_id": "tag:02NQ:proof"}
